<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE March wheat rises A$7.50 a tonne.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE March wheat rises A$7.50 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nearby March wheat gained A$7.50 to settle at A$155 a tonne on the Sydney futures Exchange on Thursday.</p>
<p>The gains came on the back of volume of 10 50-tonne lots traded in March.</p>
<p>The higher price for March wheat elevated the price of the nearby January contract by A$2.50 to A$160.50/tonne, and also reflected tight shipping schedules for exportable grains, grains traders said.</p>
<p>No other contracts were traded.  </p>
<p>The market was alo buoyed by an announcement by Pakistan on Tuesday that it is holding side-by-side tenders for 315,000 tonnes of Australian white milling wheat and U.S. soft white wheat, one trader said.</p>
